    <string name="faq_question_1">How do I fact-check a reel or short?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_1">Share an Instagram Reel or YouTube Short to Instafact from the Android share sheet, or paste the link on the home screen and tap Submit.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_2">How long does a fact-check usually take?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_2">Most checks complete in a short time, but it can take longer if the video is complex, the backend is busy, or more sources need to be reviewed.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_3">What do True, False, Misleading, and Unverified mean?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_3">True means the claim is supported by credible evidence. False means the claim is incorrect. Misleading means it mixes truth with missing context or exaggeration. Unverified means there is not enough reliable information yet.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_4">Why didn’t I receive a notification when my result was ready?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_4">Make sure notifications are allowed for Instafact on your phone. If notifications are off, the app cannot alert you when the fact-check is completed.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_5">Can I ask follow-up questions about a fact-check?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_5">Yes. Open the fact-check detail page and tap Ask Instafact AI to ask follow-up questions, understand the verdict, or explore the explanation further.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_6">Can I edit my profile photo, name, gender, or age group later?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_6">Yes. Go to Profile, tap Edit, and update your details anytime. You can also upload a new profile photo or remove the existing one.</string>
